# The observer saw #7 on world 117 circle the outsides of small rooms full of food, pressing plain wall 42 times and opening no door: the leak is spread evenly over every solid cell, so the wave pours into thick rock as readily as into a one-cell room wall where a door can be. A `thinwall` detector (a solid cell with non-solid on both sides along an axis) keeps the taught leak only on thin walls and cuts thick rock to a third, so plans lead into room walls and doors (where the per-hue leak learning then picks the door) instead of rock masses; frustration still multiplies both, so a sealed pocket can still be dug out. Built on #10 (best untuned, 27.9), the wall-thickness rule is the one change.

channel source
channel thing
channel solid
channel free
channel here
channel bad
channel leak
channel value
channel ghost: init 0
channel confinement
channel unk
channel room
channel front
channel trail: init 0
channel dwell: init 0
channel crowd: init 0
channel gateway
channel thinwall
channel conduct
channel injection

rule lay_trail:
  when 1
  set trail = max(here, 0.999 * trail)
rule dwell_time:
  when 1
  set dwell = min(1, 0.998 * dwell + 0.02 * here)
rule frustration:
  when 1
  set crowd = 0.5 * dwell + 0.5 * avg8(crowd)
rule unknown:
  when 1
  set unk = (free < 0.2) * (solid < 0.5)
rule roominess:
  when 1
  set room = 0.5 * unk + 0.5 * avg8(room)
rule frontier:
  when 1
  set front = unk * (max8(free) > 0.5)
rule gaps:
  when 1
  set gateway = max(shift(solid, 1, 0) * shift(solid, -1, 0), shift(solid, 0, 1) * shift(solid, 0, -1)) * (1 - solid)

# DOOR CANDIDATE: a solid cell only one cell thick along some axis (a room wall), not a mass of rock
rule thin_walls:
  when 1
  set thinwall = solid * max((1 - shift(solid, 1, 0)) * (1 - shift(solid, -1, 0)), (1 - shift(solid, 0, 1)) * (1 - shift(solid, 0, -1)))

rule linger:
  when 1
  set ghost = max(source, thing, 0.99 * ghost) * (1 - here) * (1 - max8(here))
rule calc_conf:
  when 1
  set confinement = sum8(solid)
rule inject:
  when 1
  set injection = max(ghost, 0.3 * front * room * room * (1 + gateway), 0.04 * unk) / (1 + 0.5 * confinement * (1 - crowd) * (1 - gateway)) * (1 - bad)

# the leak goes where a wall can open: thin walls keep their taught leak, rock mass keeps a third of it;
# frustration still raises both; known ground is trusted over unknown
rule conductance:
  when 1
  set conduct = (1 - solid * (1 - min(1, leak * (0.3 + 0.7 * thinwall) * (1 + 3 * crowd)))) * (1 - 0.08 * trail) * (1 - 0.04 * (1 - free) * (1 - solid))

rule wave:
  when 1
  set value = max(injection, max(0.94 * max4(value), 0.916214 * max8(value))) * conduct
